    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28610" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δύπτω</span></b>  (lengthd. from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δύω</span>), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>duck,
			dive</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠΰτε τις καύηξ δύπτῃσιν ἐς ἁλμυρὸν
					ὕδωρ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Antim.
					<u>Eleg.</u>
					6
				</span></i>
			 (nisi leg. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δύπτης</span>)
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">; πρὸς κῦμα δυπτούσας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lyc.
					715
				</span></i>
			: without a Prep., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔδυψε Νηρέως τάφους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					164
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νειόθι δύψας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					1.1326
				</span></i>
			: c. acc., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δύπτοντες κεφαλάς</span>
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				1008
			</span></i>.</div>
